# Workflow: DISPATCH-CHANNELS

Spec: DispatchChannels
Purpose:
  Define the dual dispatch channels for SW1 micro-units: Channel R
  (Related/Ordered) and Channel F (Free). A deterministic routing rule
  assigns each unit to exactly one channel at dispatch time. Channel F
  is scoped to the current stage ONLY; no cross-stage free dispatch is
  permitted ([SW1-1]). Every dispatch appends an entry to
  channel_routing[] in the swarm run state.

Owns: workflow/dispatch-channels.sdd

Source: DEC-2026-1011-002 (D2), extends chains/swarm.sdd SWARMCycle DISPATCH

DispatchChannels:

  channel: R | F
    R — Related/Ordered: units with depends_on run sequentially AFTER
        their dependency reaches DONE.
    F — Free: units with parallel_ready == true AND shared_state == none
        dispatch concurrently; work-stealing across free slots within
        the current stage.

  routing_rule:
    expression: channel = F iff (parallel_ready == true AND shared_state == none), else R
    deterministic: yes
    manual_assignment: SPEC VIOLATION ([DC1])

  scope:
    channel_F: current stage ONLY
    cross_stage_dispatch: FLOW VIOLATION ([SW1-1], [DC3])
    channel_R: current stage ONLY; stage order is immutable ([SW1-1])

  state:
    channel_routing[]:
      fields: unit_id, channel, timestamp, reason
      storage: .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/state.sdd (runtime-only, [R103])
      semantics: append-only; one entry per dispatch ([DC4])

  constraints:
    shared_mutable_state: forces Channel R with write-locking ([MU-3], [DC2])
    parallel_ready_false: forces Channel R regardless of shared_state
    stage_boundary: no channel may dispatch a unit of another stage

Rules:

  [DC1] Channel derivation is deterministic per the routing rule —
        manual channel assignment is a SPEC VIOLATION.
  [DC2] Channel F requires parallel_ready=true AND shared_state=none;
        any shared mutable state forces Channel R with write-locking
        ([MU-3]).
  [DC3] Channel F is scoped to the current stage — cross-stage free
        dispatch is a FLOW VIOLATION ([SW1-1]).
  [DC4] Every dispatch appends channel_routing[] (unit_id, channel,
        timestamp, reason) to the run state; the log is append-only.

Templates:
  Dispatch records live in .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/state.sdd at
  runtime (never committed, [R103]); creation uses this schema directly.

